#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example demonstrates a Simulink-controlled twin clutch front and rear differential with electrified powertrain. (Libraries > Models > Models: Simulink)
#
#CarSim support for electric powertrains includes an electric motor, electric powertrain assembly, and power management control.
#
#The vehicle in this example is AWD in which an electric motor is equipped on each of the front and rear drive axles.
#
#Browse to the Vehicle: Assembly screen and click on the powertrain blue link to see the settings for the externally controlled twin clutch front and rear differential.
#
#Click on the blue link "Differential Controller - EV" to see how the Simulink model is connected to CarSim, and how to define the import and export variables that allow CarSim and Simulink to communicate.
#
#The Procedure has open-loop controls for throttle and braking.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

